TI  - Recursion relations for scattering amplitudes with massive particles
AU  - Ballav, Sourav
AU  - Manna, Arkajyoti
T2  - Journal of High Energy Physics
AB  - We use the recently developed massive spinor-helicity formalism [1] of ArkaniHamed et al. to study a new class of recursion relations for tree-level amplitudes in gauge theories. These relations are based on a combined complex deformation of massless as well as massive external momenta. We use these relations to study tree-level amplitudes in scalar QCD as well as amplitudes involving massive vector bosons in the Higgsed phase of Yang-Mills theory. We prove the validity of our proposal by showing that in the limit of inﬁnite momenta of two of the external particles, the amplitude once again is controlled by an enhanced Spin-Lorentz symmetry paralleling the proof of BCFW shift for massless gauge theories. Simple examples illustrate that the proposed shift may lead to an eﬃcient computation of tree-level amplitudes.
